{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nOn 2026-09-01 (~12:00–16:00 PT) the Gerrit `LLM-Review` bot on host `i-00880b2c7f13527c5` (`rebar-gerrit`) fail-closed every review because clones/materializations hit `No space left on device` on the 30 GiB root disk (91–95% used), producing `VOTER_ERROR` / `coverage-gap (review-error)` vetoes. Change 2481 exhausted its retry budget to a fail-closed LLM-Review −1; 2479/2480/2482/2483 deferred. Recovery required EC2 reboot plus manual `docker builder prune -f` without `--keep-storage`, dropping disk use from ~95% to ~74%.\n\nThis is a **defect escape** of the same fail-closed-on-full-disk class as closed 2731-4c53, 7a41-95f4, 3a52-2d79, 9bc0-1200, 28f9-535c, and e2c5-f09b.\n\n## Evidence\n\nPre-prune on-box `docker system df` showed: Build Cache 5.244 GB (100% reclaimable, dominant consumer), Images 2.802 GB all active (9bc0/2340 image-retirement is working), Containers 3.572 GB, Local Volumes 947 MB, and snapshot store 1.4 GB.\n\n## Approved design\n\nThe operator approved BOTH parts on 2026-09-01; this ticket is implementation work, not an architecture decision.\n\n### Part A — acute-pressure emergency reclaim tier\n\nKeep the existing steady-state warm BuildKit cache (`BUILD_CACHE_KEEP=5GB`) for normal pressure pruning. Add `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT` (default 90, above soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT=80`). When root used-% is at or above the hard threshold, escalate `prune_docker_caches()` to `docker builder prune -f` with keep→0 (no `--keep-storage`). The action remains best-effort/non-fatal and timeout-bounded like existing docker prune calls. It must compute before/after root filesystem bytes and log bytes actually freed; an invocation marker alone is not success evidence. At normal disk levels it must keep using `--keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`.\n\n### Part B — near-full review admission control\n\nAdd a target-path free-space helper in `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py` (wrapping `shutil.disk_usage(path)`) so admission checks measure the volume that can ENOSPC, not an unrelated store volume. Add `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB` (default 2 GiB, independently documented because this is a hard pre-clone admission floor while existing janitor watermarks are cleanup targets). Check the target volume before both relevant materialization paths:\n\n1. `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` immediately before its `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")` / `gc.clone_change_ref(...)` path, using `tempfile.gettempdir()` as the measured target volume.\n2. `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` / `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py` before attested snapshot materialization, using the snapshot store path as the measured target volume.\n\nIf the target volume is below the floor, do not start the clone. For the Gerrit review-bot path, synthesize a decision carrying `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"` and route it through ADR 0069's existing `_handle_retryable_gap` bounded deferral. Add `low-disk` to `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py` `RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS` and `_TAG_SUFFIXES`, and keep `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py` classification compatible. The first-line tag remains in the `coverage-gap (<reason>)` vocabulary for the existing ADR 0069 machinery, but `low-disk` is observably distinct from `review-error` and genuine scanner/coverage gaps and must not post a vote while budget remains.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Under an induced acute-pressure condition (root used-% at or above `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT`) with enough reclaimable build-cache excess above the warm keep, automated reclaim runs the emergency keep→0 builder prune, measures `bytes_freed > 0`, logs the measured bytes, and the fixture returns root use below the soft `DISK_PRESSURE_PCT`; proof: RED/GREEN tests in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py` and/or `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py` assert before/after measurement rather than an invocation marker.\n- [ ] At normal disk levels below `DISK_PRESSURE_HARD_PCT`, `prune_docker_caches()` preserves steady-state warm-cache behavior by continuing to use `--keep-storage \"$BUILD_CACHE_KEEP\"`; proof: focused regression test in `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py`.\n- [ ] When free disk on the review-bot clone target volume is below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB`, `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py` defers the review as retryable and vote-less through ADR 0069 instead of creating the clone; proof: unit/integration test simulates low free space and asserts no clone/vote is attempted.\n- [ ] When free disk on the attested snapshot-store volume is below `REBAR_GATE_MIN_FREE_GIB`, snapshot materialization aborts before clone with a retryable low-disk condition rather than ENOSPC; proof: focused test around `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` / `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py`.\n- [ ] The low-disk admission-control condition is observably distinct from a genuine coverage/review error by using `gap_reason=\"low-disk\"`, a documented low-disk tag suffix, and tests contrasting low-disk deferral with an ordinary non-low-disk coverage gap.\n- [ ] Portability is preserved: reclaim/admission logic is in-process/operation-linked and has no dependency on a specific CI provider; proof: implementation uses shell/Python filesystem checks and existing rebar gate paths only.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n\nRun, at minimum, with the worktree virtualenv first on PATH:\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest <focused low-disk review admission/voter tests> -q`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n\n## File impact\n\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` — hard pressure tier and measured build-cache reclaim.\n- `tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py` and `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py` — RED/GREEN coverage for hard vs normal pressure behavior.\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`, `src/rebar/llm/gate_source.py` — target-volume admission helper and snapshot materialization guard.\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py`, `src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py`, `src/rebar/review_bot/retrigger.py`, `docs/review-policy.md`, and focused tests — ADR 0069 retryable vote-less low-disk deferral routing and documentation.\n\n## Provenance\n\nDiscovered during the 2026-09-01 review-bot outage triage. Related closed tickets: 9bc0-1200, 28f9-535c, e2c5-f09b, 2731-4c53, 3a52-2d79, 7a41-95f4."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788309614717795258,"uuid":"66d8b5df-3ff3-42bc-9efd-c97d82cb9619"}